senses.gloss:
स्खल् cl. 1. P. (Dhātup. xv, 37) स्खलति (rarely ˚ते; pf. चस्खाल, चस्खलुः, MBh. &c.; fut. स्खलिता, ˚लिष्यति Gr.; aor. अस्खालीत्, ib.; inf. स्खलितुम्, ib.),
to stumble, trip, totter, waver, fluctuate (with न, ‘not to waver, remain steadfast, prevail’), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to drop or slip down, trickle down, MW.;
to stammer, falter (as speech), Yājñ.; Kālid.; BhP.;
to make mistakes, blunder, err, fail, Kāv.; Car.; Rājat.;
to gather, collect, Dhātup.;
to move, MW.;
to disappear, ib. :
Caus. स्खलयति (or स्खालयति, Dhātup. xix, 59), to cause to falter, Kum.;
to stop, arrest, BhP.
